cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use radicle in your work, please cite it with the metadata below, and cite the datasets you run it on (see references)."
title: "radicle: a wheat and maize field simulator"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: MIT
authors:
  - alias: fr3on
    email: ahmed@0x200.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/fr3on/radicle"
url: "https://github.com/fr3on/radicle"
abstract: >-
  radicle simulates a wheat or maize field season in pure Python: FAO-56 reference evapotranspiration,
  a root-zone water and salt balance, growth by normalised water productivity, and weather-driven disease.
  It reads field data from CSV, DSSAT, ICASA and Excel sources and reproduces every reported result with
  one command. Most parameters are uncalibrated placeholders and each value carries a provenance label;
  maize is calibrated for one site (Greeley, Colorado) and should not be extrapolated.
keywords:
  - crop model
  - crop simulation
  - agronomy
  - evapotranspiration
  - FAO-56
  - soil salinity
  - irrigation
  - wheat
  - maize
  - reproducible research
